{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Orientation turn: read the captured OmniPaxos snapshot (core sequence_paxos, storage/batching, and the fork-added omnipaxos_runtime actor layer), set up a local offline build of the captured workspace in draft/tmp/ws to give construction-time feedback, and registered sourced questions on the decision-formation path (follower batched appends and leader decision by per-node accepted lengths) and on the recovery/resync path (AcceptSync/LogSync adoption). No defect account is claimed yet; local construction probes show basic agreement, reconfiguration StopSign, follower crash/recover catch-up and leader-change agreement all holding in a 3-node in-process cluster at batch_size=1, so the next discriminators target batching and resync orderings instead of the plain path.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"follower\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/follower.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 88,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 158,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"follower_prepare\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/follower.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 13,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 51,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"leader_accepted\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 316,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 345,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"leader_accsync\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 150,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 191,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"leader_promises\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 257,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 285,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"logsync\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/mod.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 390,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 418,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"quorum\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/util.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 131,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 259,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"batching\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 257,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 360,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"actor_unconfirmed\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 438,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 586,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"actor_notifiers\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs\\\",\n      \\\"start_line\\\": 201,\n      \\\"end_line\\\": 343,\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@batched_decided_reply\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"On a follower that receives a batched AcceptDecide, does the accepted index the follower reports back to the leader correspond to the entries it actually holds whenever the leader's decided_idx exceeds the follower's accepted_idx, so that the leader's decision index and the follower's log stay consistent?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"follower\\\", \\\"batching\\\"],\n      \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"handle_acceptdecide appends entries into the shared batch, then update_decided_idx_and_get_accepted_idx may flush the whole batch and cap decided_idx at the flushed accepted index; the index returned to the leader (reply_accepted) is the flushed length, not necessarily the length the leader assumed.\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Run a 3-node in-process cluster with batch_size > 1 and a flush_batch_tick_timeout large enough that deciding from an AcceptDecide forces the flush, then compare each node's get_decided_idx/get_accepted_idx with the content read back at those indices and with the values the leader decided on.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@resync_adoption\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"When a promise reports n_accepted greater than the leader's, or an accepted_idx beyond the leader's, does the leader adopt exactly the entries that a write quorum may have accepted, and does LogSync/AcceptSync ever truncate or reorder a decided prefix on the follower that receives it?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"follower_prepare\\\", \\\"leader_accsync\\\", \\\"logsync\\\", \\\"batching\\\"],\n      \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"The follow-up sync index for a more up-to-date follower is derived from the follower's accepted index and the leader's decided index; an off-by-one or a snapshot boundary there would let AcceptSync overwrite entries the follower had accepted or already decided.\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Construct an up-to-date follower (accepted but not decided entries from an earlier ballot) and a leader with a shorter log, force the Prepare/AcceptSync exchange, and compare the follower's decided prefix and entry content at the reported indices before and after the exchange.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@quorum_lengths\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Are the accept-phase support counts in the captured code computed over per-node accepted log lengths, and is that the same quantity the decide step and trim step assume?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"quorum\\\", \\\"leader_accepted\\\", \\\"batching\\\"],\n      \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"is_chosen counts nodes with accepted_indexes >= idx where accepted_indexes holds log lengths (accepted_idx), and the leader passes a length to it; a consumer that treated the value as a 0-based entry index would be off by one.\\\",\n      \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Read the leader's decide step and trim step together with the definition of accepted_idx in state_cache/internal_storage, and confirm whether every producer and consumer of that number uses length semantics.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\npython3 -c \\\"import json;json.load(open('update.json'));print('ok')\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
